          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Atlas management credentials and database-user credentials serve separate purposes: automation needs control-plane authentication, while database users created by provisioning commands authenticate application or shell connections to the database. (high confidence) Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/cli/current/atlas-cli-temporary-cluster.md ; https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-add-mongodb-users.md",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/cli/current/atlas-cli-temporary-cluster.md",
          "note": null,
